hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1433","It was narrated that Ya'la bin Umayyah said:\"\"I said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'There is no sin on you if you shorten salah and if you fear that the disbelievers may put you in trial (attack you). But now the people are safe.' 'Umar said: 'I wondered the same thing"
"1434","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out from Makkah to Al-Madinah"
"1435","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"\"We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) between Makkah and Al-Madinah"
"1436","It was narrated that Ibn Al-Simt said:\"\"I saw 'Umar bin Al-Khattab praying two rak'ahs in Dhul-Hulaifah and I asked him about that. He said: 'I am simply doing that which I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) doing"
"1437","It was narrated that Anas said:\"\"I went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Al-Madinah to Mekkah"
"1438","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:\"\"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey"
"1439","It was narrated that 'Umar said:\"\"The prayer for jumu'ah is two rak'ahs"
"1440","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"\"The prayer of the resident was enjoined on the tongue of your Prophet (ﷺ)"
"1441","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:\"The prayer of the resident was enjoined on the tongue of your Prophet (ﷺ), four (rak'ahs), and the prayer of the traveler is two rak'ahs, and the prayer of fear is one rak'ah.\""
"1442","It was narrated that Qatadah said:\"\"I heard Muas- bin Salamah-say: 'I said to Ibn 'Abbas: How should I pray in Makkah if I do not pray in congregation? He said: Two rak'ahs"
"1443","Musa bin Salamah narrated that he asked Ibn 'Abbas:\"\"I missed the prayer in congregation when I was in Al-Batha; how do you think I should pray?\"\" He said: \"\"Two rak'ahs"
"1444","It was narrated that Harithah bin Wahab Al-Khuza'i said:\"\"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Mina when the people were more secure and greater in number"
"1445","It was narrated that Harithah bin Wahab said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in prayer in Mina"
"1446","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that he said:\"\"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Mina"
"1447","It was narrated that 'Abdullah (ﷺ) said:\"\"I prayed two rak'ahs in Mina with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1448","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid said:\"\"Uthman prayer four (rak'ahs) in Mina until news of that reached 'Abdullah who said: 'I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1449","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:\"\"I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Mina"
"1450","Ubaidullah bin 'Abdullah bin Umar narrated that:His father said: \"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rak'ahs in Mina"
"1451","It was narrated from Yahya bin Abi Ishaq that :Anas bin Malik said: \"\" We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Al-Madinah to Makkah and he used to lead us in praying two rak'ahs until we came back.\"\" I (Yahya) said: \"\"Did he stay in Makkah?\"\" He (Anas) said: \"\"Yes"
"1452","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed in Makkah (for fifteen days)"
"1453","Al-'Ala bin Al-Hadrami said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The Muhajir may stay for three days after completing his rituals"
"1454","It was narrated that Al-'Ala bin Al-Hadrami said:\"\"The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'The Muhajir may stay for three days after his rituals"
"1455","It was narrated from 'Aishah that:She performed Umrah with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1456","Wabarah bin Abdur-Rahman said:\"\"Ibn 'Umar did not offer more than two rak'ahs when traveling"
"1457","Eisa bin Hafs bin 'Asim said:\"\"My father told me: 'I was with Ibn Umar on a journey"
"1458","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:\"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The sun and moon are two signs of Allah (SWT)"
